          %h2#the_idea The idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %em separable algebras
            is a strengthening of the concept of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+algebras"} semisimple algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+field+extensions"} separable field extensions
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            There are a several equivalent characterizations of separable algebras. For all of these we fix a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital+algebra"} unital
          %p
            First, a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is defined to be
            %strong separable
            if for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+extension"} field extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi k
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes_k K
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+algebra"} semisimple
          %p
            Second, a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is separable if and only if it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+module"} flat
            when considered as a right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi e
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^e = A \otimes_k A^{op}
            in the obvious (but perhaps not quite standard) way.
          %p
            Third, a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is separable if and only if it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective
            when considered as a left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^e
            in the usual way.
          %p
            Fourth, a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is separable if and only if the
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^e
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi m
                          %mo :
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mi e
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi b
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                          %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  m : &amp; A^e &amp;\to &amp; A  \\
                  \&amp; a \otimes b &amp; \mapsto &amp; a b
                  }
          %p
            has a right inverse, that is a
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^e
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to  A^e
          %p
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m f = 1_A
          %p
            It is easy to see that the third and fourth definitions are equivalent. We have an epimorphism of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^e
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi e
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi m
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^e \stackrel{m}{\longrightarrow} A \to 0
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            as above exists, this splits, so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a summand of a free
            = succeed "-module," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^e
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^e
            itself, so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is projective as an
            = succeed "-module." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^e
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is projective, any epimorphism to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            splits.
          %p
            We can also state the fourth characterization in a more grungy way in terms of the element
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = f(1)
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is separable if and only if there exists an element
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = \sum_{i=1}^n a_i \otimes b_i  \in A^e
          %p such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i=1}^n a_i b_i = 1
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mi p
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a p = p a
          %p
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is called a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong separability idempotent
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^2 = p
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#classification Classification
          %p
            There is a classification theorem for separable algebras: separable algebras are the same as finite products of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+algebras"} matrix algebras
            over finite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+algebras"} division algebras
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/centers"} centers
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+field+extension"} separable field extensions
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+field"} perfect field
            is one for which every extension is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+field+extension"} separable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a perfect field, separable algebras are the same as finite products of matrix algebras over finite-dimensional division algebras over field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a perfect field, there is no difference between a separable algebra over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            and a finite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+algebra"} semisimple algebra
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %h3#RelationToFrobeniusAlgebras Relation to Frobenius algebras
          %p
            A result of
            %a{:href => "#EilenbergNakayama55"} Eilenberg &amp; Nakayama (1955)
            states that any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+algebra"} separable algebra
            over a field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            can be given the structure of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+algebra"} symmetric Frobenius algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            of a Frobenius algebra is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} dual
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#EilenbergNakayama55"} Eilenberg &amp; Nakayama (1955)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#EndoWatanabe67"} Endo &amp; Watanabe (1967), in particular Thm. 4.2.
          %p
            A separable algebra is said to be
            %strong strongly separable
            if there exists a separability idempotent
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            that is
            = succeed "," do
              %strong symmetric
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mi i
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = \sum_{i=1}^n a_i \otimes b_i = \sum_{i=1}^n b_i \otimes a_i
          %p
            An algebra is strongly separable if and only if it can be made into a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+algebra"} special Frobenius algebra
          %p
            There is an equivalent characterization of strongly separable algebras which makes this fact clearer. Any element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            of an associative unital algebra gives a left multiplication map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mi a
                          %mo :
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi b
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                          %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  L_a : &amp;A &amp;\to&amp; A \\
                  \&amp;b &amp;\mapsto&amp; a b
                  }
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is finite-dimensional, there is a bilinear pairing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: A \times A \to k
            defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(a,b) = tr(L_a L_b)
          %p
            An algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is strongly separable if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %strong nondegenerate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to A^*
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \mapsto g(a, -)
          %p
            In this case, there is just one way to make
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            into a special Frobenius algebra, namely by defining the counit to be
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon(a) = tr(L_a)
          %p Here are some examples of strongly separable algebras:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the algebra of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ×
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \times n
                matrices with entries in a field
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                is always separable, but it is strongly separable if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                is not divisible by the characteristic of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %li
              %p
                the group algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[G]
                of a finite group is strongly separable if and only if the order of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is not divisible by the characteristic of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p For more details, see Aguiar’s note below.
          %h3#over_commutative_rings Over commutative rings
          %p
            More generally, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital+ring"} unital
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is projective as a module over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^e = A \otimes_k A^{op}
          %p
            As in the case of algebras over a field, an algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            over a commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is separable if and only if the
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^e
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mi e
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi b
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                          %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  m \colon &amp; A^e &amp;\to &amp; A
                  \\\
                  \&amp; a \otimes b &amp; \mapsto &amp; a b
                  }
          %p splits, and this in turn is equivalent to the existence of a separability idempotent.
          %p
            If a separable algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is also projective as a module over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-module." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            If the center of a separable algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            over a commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is called an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Azumaya+algebra"} Azumaya algebra
          %h3#separable_extensions_of_noncommutative_rings Separable extensions of noncommutative rings
          %p
            The ring extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is said to be a separable extension if all short exact sequences of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "-bimodules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "-bimodules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "-bimodules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi HH
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo ;
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HH^n(S,R;M) = 0
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\gt 0
            and all coefficient bimodules
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %h3#in_algebraic_geometry In algebraic geometry
          %p
            Commutative separable algebras play an important role in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+morphism"} étale cover
            is a way of implementing the idea of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+ring"} spectrum
            of a field corresponds to a commutative separable algebra over that field. Lieven Le Bruyn has written “in categorical terms, studying the monoidal category of commutative separable
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed ":" do
              %em fundamental theorem of Grothendieck Galois theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is contravariantly equivalent to the category of continuous actions on finite sets of the profinite fundamental group of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %em profinite fundamental group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is the Galois group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gal(k_s|k)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_s
            is a
            %em separable closure
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+field+extension"} separable field extension
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            Separable algebras play a major role in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
            of extensions of algebras. There are further generalizations, leading to
            = succeed "\u2026" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+functor"} separable functors
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+functor"} separable functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+field+extension"} separable field extension
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+coring"} separable coring
          %h2#References References
          %ul
            %li#EilenbergNakayama55
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Eilenberg"}> Samuel Eilenberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadasi+Nakayama"} Tadasi Nakayama
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the dimension of modules and algebras. II. Frobenius algebras and quasi-Frobenius rings
                %em Nagoya Math. J.
                %strong 9
                (1955) 1-16 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/nagoya-mathematical-journal/volume-9/issue-none/On-the-dimension-of-modules-and-algebras-II-Frobenius-algebras/nmj/1118799677.pdf"}> euclid
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                K. Hirata, K. Sugano,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On semisimple and separable extensions of noncommutative rings
            %li#EndoWatanabe67
              %p
                Shizuo Endo, Yutaka Watanabe,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On separable algebras over a commutative ring
                %em Osaka J. Math.
                = succeed "(2)" do
                  %strong 4
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/download/pdf_1/euclid.ojm/1200691953"} euclid
            %li
              %p
                F. DeMeyer and E. Ingraham,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Separable algebras over commutative rings
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 181
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcelo+Aguiar"}> Marcelo Aguiar
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A note on strongly separable algebras
                %strong 65
                (2000) 51-60 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.cornell.edu/~maguiar/strongly.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Separable_algebra"} Separable algebra
          %p
            An explicit proof of the Grothendieck Galois theory statement that the category of commutative separable algebras over a field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is anti-equivalent to the category of continuous actions on finite sets of the profinite fundamental group of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %ul
            %li
              Federico G. Lastaria,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On separable algebras in Grothendieck Galois theory
              %a{:href => "http://www.dmi.unict.it/ojs/index.php/lematematiche/article/view/464/0"} link
